    <p>Some tools I have built, for research and for fun.</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="https://libmat.ningnawang.workers.dev/">LibMAT</a>: a C++ library with Python bindings and optional CUDA support for computing the 3D medial axis transform of triangle and tetrahedral meshes.</li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/songshibo/blender-mat-addon">Blender MAT Add-on</a>: a Blender add-on for importing medial meshes (.ma files) and building interpolated medial axis transforms, made with <a href="https://songshibo.github.io/">Shibo Song</a>.</li>
        <li><a href="https://how2split.ningnawang.workers.dev/">How2split</a>: a free service that helps a group of friends split shared trip expenses, inspired by <a href="https://www.when2meet.com/">When2meet</a>.</li>
    </ul>
